\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Physical PVB continuous frame structure and spectral bounds. (a) Peak-normalized radial intensity $I(r)/I_{\max }$ for physical PVBs ($w/R_0 = 0.15$, solid) across $l = 0,2,4,6$ versus $\mathrm  {LG}_{0,l}$ ($w_0 = R_0$, dashed); inset compares the exact transcendental differential shift $\Delta r_{\mathrm  {peak}}(l)/R_0$ ($w/R_0 = 0.25$, circles) against $(l^2/8)(w/R_0)^4$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:peak_shift}]. (b) Unit-normalized radial overlap $\gamma _l(R_0, R_0+\Delta R)$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:gamma_normalized}] at $R_0 = 4w$ for $l = 0,1,4$ versus the $l$-independent Gaussian asymptote $e^{-\Delta R^2/(2w^2)}$ (dotted), marking $13.6\%$ at $\Delta R = 2.0\,w$ and $4.40\%$ at $\Delta R = 2.5\,w$; inset confirms azimuthal Kronecker orthogonality $\delta _{l,l'}$. (c) Continuous-frame Fourier multiplier $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle G$}\mathaccent "0365{G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with Paley--Wiener passband $\mathcal  {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.394$; inset shows the deconvolution noise gain $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ peaking at $(2\sqrt  {\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}})^{-1}$. (d) Sharp Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B = 1$ and condition number $\kappa (S_{w,k_{\max }})$ versus $w k_{\max }$, annotating both the low-NA reference ($w k_{\max } = 0.604 \DOTSB \tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\DOTSB \Relbar \joinrel \Rightarrow \tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}A = 0.833, \kappa = 1.20$) and the telecom RCF benchmark ($\lambda = 1550\,\mathrm  {nm}, \mathrm  {NA} = 0.20, w = 1.72\,\mu \mathrm  {m}$: $w k_{\max } = 1.394 \DOTSB \tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\DOTSB \Relbar \joinrel \Rightarrow \tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}A = 0.378, \kappa = 2.64$).}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frame_spectrum}{{1}{4}{Physical PVB continuous frame structure and spectral bounds. (a) Peak-normalized radial intensity $I(r)/I_{\max }$ for physical PVBs ($w/R_0 = 0.15$, solid) across $l = 0,2,4,6$ versus $\mathrm {LG}_{0,l}$ ($w_0 = R_0$, dashed); inset compares the exact transcendental differential shift $\Delta r_{\mathrm {peak}}(l)/R_0$ ($w/R_0 = 0.25$, circles) against $(l^2/8)(w/R_0)^4$ [Eq.~\eqref {eq:peak_shift}]. (b) Unit-normalized radial overlap $\gamma _l(R_0, R_0+\Delta R)$ [Eq.~\eqref {eq:gamma_normalized}] at $R_0 = 4w$ for $l = 0,1,4$ versus the $l$-independent Gaussian asymptote $e^{-\Delta R^2/(2w^2)}$ (dotted), marking $13.6\%$ at $\Delta R = 2.0\,w$ and $4.40\%$ at $\Delta R = 2.5\,w$; inset confirms azimuthal Kronecker orthogonality $\delta _{l,l'}$. (c) Continuous-frame Fourier multiplier $\widetilde {G}_w(k_\perp )$ and Tikhonov transfer $T_{\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ ($\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}} = 10^{-2}, 10^{-3}$) with Paley--Wiener passband $\mathcal {H}_{k_{\max }}$ shaded up to $w k_{\max } = 1.394$; inset shows the deconvolution noise gain $\widetilde {H}_{w,\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}}(k_\perp )$ peaking at $(2\sqrt {\alpha _{\mathrm {reg}}})^{-1}$. (d) Sharp Paley--Wiener bounds $A(w,k_{\max }), B = 1$ and condition number $\kappa (S_{w,k_{\max }})$ versus $w k_{\max }$, annotating both the low-NA reference ($w k_{\max } = 0.604 \implies A = 0.833, \kappa = 1.20$) and the telecom RCF benchmark ($\lambda = 1550\,\mathrm {nm}, \mathrm {NA} = 0.20, w = 1.72\,\mu \mathrm {m}$: $w k_{\max } = 1.394 \implies A = 0.378, \kappa = 2.64$)}{figure.1}{}}
