\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Laguerre--Gaussian expansion, radial washout, regularized noisy reconstruction, and discrete Gram conditioning. (a) Closed-form coefficients $c_{1,p}(R)$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:c_lp_exact}, solid] versus adaptive quadrature (circles) for $\mathrm  {LG}_{p,1}$ ($p = 0\text  {--}3$, $w/w_0 = 0.25$); inset shows $\log _{10}\lvert \Delta c\rvert  < -14$. (b) Nodal washout fidelity $\mathcal  {F}(p,1,w/w_0)$ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:fidelity_fourier}] with Table~\ref {tab:fidelity} values (dots); inset compares exact $\mathcal  {F} = 0.95$ roots $w_{\mathrm  {crit}}/w_0$ ($p = 0\text  {--}8$) against $0.573/\sqrt  {2p+\lvert l\rvert +1}$ ($l = 1$). (c) Noisy $\mathrm  {LG}_{2,1}$ reconstruction error ($w/w_0 = 0.25$, $w k_{\max } = 3.0$, bandlimited white noise power $P_\varepsilon = 0.01$, input $\mathrm  {SNR} = 20\,\mathrm  {dB}$) decomposed into analytical $\mathrm  {Bias}^2$ and variance alongside $256\times 256$ 2D-FFT Monte Carlo trials (circles, $\pm 1\,\mathrm  {SEM}$), reducing unregularized error $\mathrm  {MSE}(\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}} = 0) = 9.002$ to $\mathrm  {MSE}_{\min } = 0.03481$ at $\alpha _{\mathrm  {reg}}^{\mathrm  {opt}} = 0.04902$ ($258.6\times $ suppression). (d) Monotonic unit-normalized $\kappa (\gamma )$ versus diverging unnormalized $\kappa (G)$ (left axis) and adjacent power crosstalk $\lvert \gamma _{12}\rvert ^2$ in dB (right axis) for Table~\ref {tab:gram_matrix}.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
